From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:16:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: the alchemy command, composing alchemy, transduce and
 render

On the maintainer's instruction of 2026-10-04, alchemy owns the shared
types and takes its routers and renderers from its host
(tabnas/alchemy#40), and the command moves here: the one place that
builds all three, passing transduce's Routers (tabnas/transduce#32) and
render's Renderers (tabnas/render#13) to alchemy's compile.

- TypeScript: @tabnas/alchemy-cli, the `alchemy` bin.
- Go: github.com/tabnas/alchemy-cli/go, cmd/alchemy.
- Rust: tabnas-alchemy-cli, the `alchemy` binary.

Each carries the CLI tests that moved out of alchemy. CI: the fleet's
polyglot workflow (ci.yml, with a go-nodecell job), the Rust gate
(rust.yml running ci/rust/run.sh and ci/polyglot/run.sh against sibling
checkouts) and the dependency gate.

